# Passwordless sudo for the runner user.
#
# Ascender jobs arrive over receptor and run as uid 1000 (ascender). They need
# root inside the container to drive podman-remote and to install packages
# during a play. The base image's packaged /etc/sudoers enables %wheel with a
# password prompt, which a non-interactive job has no way to answer.
#
# Granted to the user, not to %wheel: a group-based grant silently extends to
# any future member of that group.
#
# This is a drop-in on purpose. The previous approach replaced the whole of
# /etc/sudoers, which the sudo package owns and reverts on update.
ascender ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
